# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal product thinking — deliberately NOT shared.
#
# What stays in the repo is what somebody needs in order to RUN, BUILD or
# INTEGRATE with this app: README.md, TECH.md, docs/build-status.md and
# docs/qa/. Everything below is our own working material — ideas, competitor
# research, screen audits, meeting agendas. It changes weekly, it is argued
# over, and it is noise to anyone pulling this repo to build against it.
#
# TWO DELIBERATE EXCEPTIONS, both added after this rule proved too broad:
# `docs/decision-log.md` and `docs/superpowers/specs/`. Tracked code cites
# them by name — `pairing/types.ts` carries a field "per D31",
# `AppHeader.tsx` defers a blur pending "spec open item 7" — and a comment
# that points at a file nobody else can open is a dead reference. An approved
# spec is a decision record, not a draft: it belongs with the code whose shape
# it explains, the same way `docs/build-status.md` does.
#
# These files still exist on disk; they are simply no longer tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/PRODUCT.md
docs/product/
docs/research/
docs/audit/
docs/discussion-guide.md

# Execution scratch — regenerated per phase, superseded the moment it is run.
docs/superpowers/plans/

example

# generated native folders
/ios
/android
